course: dictionary
lesson: 14643
title: A precedent is an example from the past
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A precedent is something that happened before, which people use as an example when they decide what to do next time. «The school let us bring pets on sports day, so that is a precedent for next year.» Next year, people will look back and think: we did it before, so we can do it again.
explain: Precedent is a noun, so you can say a precedent or precedents. In formal writing, the adjective form is used to mean something that has no earlier example. «The flood was without precedent in the town's history» means nothing like it had ever happened there before.
explain: Judges in court use precedent a lot. Earlier decisions in similar cases guide the judge, so that people are treated fairly and in the same way. When you meet this word, ask yourself: has something like this happened before, and what happened then?
fact: A precedent is an action or decision from the past that is used as an example later.
fact: In law, a precedent is an earlier judgement in court that judges follow in similar cases.
fact: «Set a precedent» means to do something that others will later copy or follow.
fact: «Without precedent» means it has never happened before.
fact: Parents may worry that letting one child stay up late sets a precedent for the others.
exercise: «The head teacher let us wear hats in the snow. This set a precedent.» What does precedent mean here? | A hat made of snow | A cold morning | A rule that stops you playing outside | *An example from the past that others may follow later
exercise: «The flood was without precedent in the town's history.» What does without precedent mean? | *It had never happened before | It happened every single year | It was only a little bit wet | It was small and quiet
exercise: Dad says, «Letting you stay up late once would set a precedent.» Why might he say that? | He is talking about a famous old judge | He wants you to go to bed right now, this minute | *He thinks it would be copied as an example next time | He likes you to sleep in a big bed
test: «The judges followed an old precedent when they decided the case.» What is a precedent here? | A kind of school exam | A ruined old building | *An earlier decision in a similar case that guides the judge | A new law made this morning
test: Ella says, «Breaking with precedent, we will hold the party in the park.» What does break with precedent mean? | Break a plate by accident | Stop the party early | Ask for permission twice | *Do something differently from what was done before
exam: «The judges followed an old precedent when they decided the case.» Which is the best meaning of precedent here? | *An earlier decision that guides a similar case | A famous old judge | A ruined old building | A kind of school exam
